     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe and I want to check it with you first.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. That's twice the labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is **2550 mg/day**. The maximum for extended-release is 2000 mg/day. Doses that high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI side effects, even with normal kidney function.\n\n**What you may have meant:**\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the IR maximum), or\n- **1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and tell me why, and I'll put the reason in a note on the order."
      }
